- Are there any protective orders, sealing requests, or confidentiality procedures we should seek because of sensitive custody/financial information?

B — Key questions to ask Maria Santos (to prepare you and set strategy)
- What questions is the judge most likely to ask me at this particular type of hearing?
- What questions will opposing counsel likely ask me during depositions or at trial?
- What facts or documents do you want me to bring and in what format (timeline, exhibit binder, electronic copies)?
- What is our theory of the case and the specific legal grounds for enforcement/defense of the NDA (e.g., breach, invalidity, overbreadth, unconscionability, waiver)?
- How should I describe the NDA terms (scope, duration, definition of confidential information) in plain language?
- How do custody/financial matters affect the case and what information must we disclose vs. keep confidential?
- Are there any privilege issues (attorney-client or work product) or evidence we should not produce? Should we prepare a privilege log?
- Do we need any expert witnesses (e.g., damages expert, forensic analyst)? If so, who and by when?
