F — Tips for answering questions and courtroom/deposition conduct
- Consult Maria before the hearing about what you can say on the record. If unsure, ask for a brief break.
- Answer only the question asked. Keep responses short and factual. Don’t volunteer extra information.
- If you don’t know or can’t recall, say “I don’t recall” rather than guessing.
