A. Key questions to ask your attorney (Maria Santos)
- Case posture and timeline
  - What exactly will happen at the upcoming preliminary hearing (case management conference, preliminary injunction hearing, or something else)?
  - What are the critical near-term deadlines (papers to file, discovery deadlines, hearing dates)?
  - Is this likely to proceed to trial, or do you recommend settlement/mediation before that?
- Legal theory & defenses
  - Under what legal theory are we pursuing the NDA dispute (breach of contract, injunctive relief, trade secret claims, etc.)?
  - What defenses do you expect the respondent to raise (unenforceability, overbreadth, lack of consideration, waiver, estoppel)?
- Relief and burden
  - What relief are we asking for at the preliminary hearing (temporary restraining order, preliminary injunction, case scheduling, etc.)?
  - What is the burden of proof for the relief we seek, and what specific facts do we need to show?
- Evidence & admissibility
  - Which documents and witnesses are most important to prove breach and damages?
  - Are any documents protected by privilege or sensitive (custody/financial records)? If so, how will we present them (redaction, sealing, in camera review, protective order)?
  - Do we need expert witnesses (forensic accountant, damages expert, IT expert for data access)?
