- Draft/seek a protective order and request to seal sensitive family records if needed
- Identify discovery requests and subpoenas to pursue now
- Propose a witness/exhibit list for the upcoming hearing
- Run a mock Q&A and prepare a written “talking points” sheet for you
- Discuss cost projections and will the firm advance costs

Other practical tips
