Questions to ask your attorney (Maria Santos)
- Case posture and immediate goals
  - What exactly will be decided at the upcoming hearing and what should our objectives be?
  - What is the likely timeline from this hearing to trial (or settlement)?
  - Are there administrative deadlines or local rules in San Diego County I need to know about now?

- Evidence and proof
  - What specific evidence do we need to prove breach/non-breach of the NDA?
  - Which documents are most important and how should they be authenticated?
  - Are there hearsay, authentication, or privilege risks with any of my documents or communications?

- Discovery and disclosures
  - What discovery has been requested and what remains outstanding (interrogatories, requests for production, depositions)?
  - What are our obligations and deadlines for providing documents or witness lists?
  - Should we seek a protective order or confidentiality order? If so, how and when?

- Legal issues and defenses
  - What are the strongest legal theories for our side (e.g., breach, enforceability, limitation, ambiguity, waiver, public interest exceptions)?
  - What defenses or counterclaims can the respondent raise (e.g., invalidity, lack of consideration, unconscionability, prior disclosure)?
  - Are there local/state law nuances in California or San Diego County that materially affect the case?

- Remedies and risks
  - What remedies are we asking for (injunction, damages, fees)? What is realistic?
  - What is the exposure (monetary, injunctive relief, sanctions) if the judge rules against us?
  - Could custody or financial matters be used to attack my credibility or increase alleged damages?

- Witnesses and testimony
  - Which witnesses should we call or depose? Which witnesses does the respondent likely rely on?
  - Should I expect to testify at the hearing or at trial? If so, what will I be asked and how should I prepare?
  - Are there expert witnesses we should retain (for damages, forensic analysis, employment practices)?

- Privilege, confidentiality and communications
  - Are any communications privileged (attorney-client, work-product)? How should I preserve privilege?
  - Should we seal documents or file under seal to protect confidential information?
  - How do we handle communications with third parties, social media, or the press?

- Strategy & settlement
  - What settlement parameters are acceptable (monetary, injunctive terms, confidentiality)?
  - Should we engage in mediation now or wait until after the hearing?
  - How should we respond if opposing counsel offers a last-minute settlement?

- Practical and procedural
  - Who will speak in court? Will you (Maria) argue or will I need to be present and speak?
  - What should I bring to court and how should I behave during the hearing?
  - Are there any sanctions or filing requirements I should worry about?

Questions the judge may ask (preliminary hearing / case management / motion)
- Procedural / case status
  - What relief are you requesting and what is your legal basis?
  - What factual issues are in dispute and what issues can be narrowed now?
  - How long will trial take and what is an appropriate trial date?
  - Have the parties complied with discovery and meet-and-confer requirements?

- Evidence and urgency (especially for injunction/TRO)
  - Is there an imminent risk of harm that justifies emergency relief?
  - What evidence supports irreparable harm and why are damages insufficient?
  - Are there less burdensome alternatives to the relief you seek?

- Confidentiality and public interest
  - Are there privacy/confidentiality concerns that warrant sealing or redaction?
  - Will granting relief affect third parties or the public interest?

Questions opposing counsel (or the judge through opposing counsel) is likely to ask you (during hearing, deposition, or trial)
- Formation and terms of the NDA
  - Did you sign the NDA? When and under what circumstances?
  - Can you identify the specific provisions at issue (what text, what dates, what parties)?
  - Did you receive any separate disclosures or explanations about the NDA’s scope?

- Alleged breach facts
  - What exactly did you disclose (what information, to whom, when)?
  - How did the disclosure happen (email, phone, casual conversation, publication)?
  - Were any of the disclosed items already public or independently known?

